      en: "The Metaliferi Mountains are a range in the Apuseni Mountains, Romania, known for their ore wealth. The highest peak is Detunata Goală at 1,377 m. The range consists of volcanic rocks (andesite, dacite) from Tertiary volcanism. Historically, gold, silver, copper, and zinc were mined; Romans worked the ores here. The landscape is dotted with old adits and tailings. Vegetation includes beech and oak forests. The region is a center of Romanian mining, with towns like Brad and Abrud. Today most mines are closed; tourism is growing.",
